# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A LINE. Vercel does NOT read .gitignore — without this
# file it uploads essentially the whole working tree. On 2026-08-10 the first
# production deploy of the platform changes reported an 8.5 GB upload before it
# was cancelled: `.turbo` alone was 16 GB on disk and `cli/dist` 1.1 GB, none of
# which the build reads.
#
# The rule for a new line: it belongs here only if the build REGENERATES it or
# never reads it. Source, config and workspace manifests must NOT be listed —
# both projects deploy from the repo root and Vercel applies each project's own
# Root Directory setting, so an over-broad pattern here breaks the build for
# every app at once.

# Local build caches — regenerated, and by far the largest thing on disk.
.turbo
**/.turbo

# Installed by Vercel itself during the build.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Next.js build output — Vercel builds fresh.
.next
**/.next

# Compiled Go binaries for five platforms. The `bk` CLI is released through
# GitHub + npm (devops/release.sh cli), never through a web deploy.
cli/dist
cli/bk

# Test and tooling artefacts.
coverage
**/coverage
*.log

# The sales-app build's agent/human correspondence. Not code.
salesImplementation
